  "source_findings": [
    "GpuPlan CFV/worklist/river arrays and node-scalar/dense-owner arrays have independent post-DFS immutable inputs but would require concurrency/peak/lifetime qualification. No parallel candidate created or gain inferred.",
    "Show worklists currently append node IDs in ascending order within levels, before river slots are assigned. Both training and evaluation launch up_show using these fixed per-level spans.",
    "up_show reads reach and immutable metadata, and each terminal writes its own persistent CFV row. It does not read the CFV buffer. Reordering distinct show nodes within the same stream launch preserves per-node arithmetic and inter-kernel dependency order.",
    "No applicable show-by-river ordering candidate found in bounded current ledger, preserved Rust source or local all-ref plan history searches; not exhaustive remote history.",
    "Different GPU block scheduling, reach/output locality and added CPU sort cost could erase any immutable-table locality advantage; no hardware cache counter or predicted speedup."
  ],
